1
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,240
Summer has come again this year.

2
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,920
It's here, it's here,
it's really here, it's here, it's here!

3
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,160
Summer has come again this year.

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,680
It's here, it's really here,
it's here, it's here!

5
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,780
On the big road,
we drink it all up, every last drop.

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:31,600
On the big road,
we drink it all up, every last drop.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,580
On the big road,
we drink it all up, every last drop.

8
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:35,980
Agesame

9
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,000
Summer has come again this year.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,660
It's here, it's really here,
it's here, it's here!

11
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,440
A big sea, small waves, tiny little ones.

12
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:55,260
Riding the south wind,

13
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:58,440
big bottoms, small bottoms,
tiny little ones.

14
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,900
Riding the south wind,

15
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:08,700
Riding the south wind,

16
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,560
Riding the south wind,

17
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:20,580
on the shore, lazy and dreamy,
on the shore, lazy and dreamy.

18
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:31,660
with shaved ice, we love it, we love it.

19
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,809
Alright,

20
00:01:39,859 --> 00:01:43,982
it's this hot already in the morning,

21
00:01:44,032 --> 00:01:46,680
it's unbearable, I tell you.

22
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:53,060
Shaved ice, strawberry, please.

23
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:54,160
Coming right up.

24
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,420
Since when did you
switch to an electric one?

25
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,198
Since this year, see.
The electric one's easier,

26
00:02:02,248 --> 00:02:04,160
and it doesn't stiffen your shoulders.

27
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,360
Well, obviously.

28
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,820
Yeah, I figured I'd toss
that old one out too.

29
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,360
You're throwing it away? What a waste.

30
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,920
This ice shaver still
has plenty of life left.

31
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,860
Well, it's the way of the times.
Here you go.

32
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,900
If you don't need it,
I'll take it off your hands.

33
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,340
Yeah, sure.

34
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,420
Auntie!

35
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:28,980
Melon flavor?

36
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,040
Here you go.

37
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:37,900
You kids, if you just wait for vacation without studying,
your mom's gonna scold you.

38
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,700
Shouldn't you be the one slacking off here,
Ryo-san?

39
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,980
I'm not slacking off, I'm eating shaved ice.

40
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:50,740
These days,
even brats like you talk like the Chief.

41
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,560
Done eating, done eating.

42
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:02,360
On days you eat cold stuff,
wrap your belly up before you sleep.

43
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,900
Don't come crying to me if you get
an upset stomach and have the runs.

44
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,100
Well, I'm taking this one then.

45
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,000
Here you go, then.

46
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,660
The working-class general
gasping in this scorching hell!

47
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,680
Ryo-chan, what's that?

48
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:22,860
I got this original ice
shaver from the dagashi shop.

49
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:27,700
An ice shaver? You'll take anything they give you,
won't you, senpai?

50
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:32,800
What are you planning to do with that?

51
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,360
What do you think? I'm obviously
going to make shaved ice with it.

52
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,980
In winter,
it's kotatsu and mandarin oranges.

53
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,860
In summer, it's the bench and shaved ice.

54
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,080
Even if I grate katsuobushi with this,
there's no harm in that, is there?

55
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,640
Senpai, if it's an ice shaver,

56
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:49,700
Ryo-chan bought one at a
supermarket sale last week.

57
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,200
Well, look at this Pen-kichi-kun.

58
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:56,160
Something like that toy won't do.

59
00:03:56,700 --> 00:04:00,140
In this gourmet age,
even shaved ice has to be the real thing.

60
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,800
Is there such a thing
as authentic shaved ice?

61
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,760
It keeps changing depending
on the time and place.

62
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:09,600
You were showing off this
shaver until last week, though.

63
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,760
I'll make some right away!

64
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,418
But Ryo-chan,

65
00:04:13,468 --> 00:04:17,040
If you're talking authentic,
I suppose you won't use fridge ice.

66
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:24,140
If you're going for authentic, it has to be Mont
Blanc ice or Antarctic ice, at the very least.

67
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,140
Antarctic ice

68
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:29,700
Nakagawa Concern has a branch in Greenland,

69
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,680
so we could get Arctic ice.

70
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:34,580
That's it!

71
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,720
For gourmet shaved ice,
Arctic beats Antarctic!

72
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:40,440
Buy that ice and get
it delivered right away.

73
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,340
Well, sure, but...

74
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,580
Listen, I want it right now!

75
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,660
I hate waiting, you know.

76
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:47,840
Understood.

77
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,640
Well then, I'll go take a break.

78
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:53,640
He always gets serious so quickly.

79
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:05,680
What, I can't even
sleep with all this noise.

80
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,220
Senior,
the ice from headquarters has arrived.

81
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,520
The ice came quickly!

82
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,500
It's here.

83
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,540
Where's the ice?

84
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,190
A whole block of ice

85
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,940
Yes! All of this is mine!

86
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,760
Alright, here,
ten thousand yen for the shaving.

87
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:38,120
Over here a little more this way.

88
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,020
There.

89
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,400
Yahoo!

90
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,960
This is going to be a lot of food!

91
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,760
Ugh, it's hot.

92
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:03,260
Of all times for the AC to break,
this is the worst.

93
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:05,740
It feels like it should be snowing,
doesn't it?

94
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,620
Right?

95
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,920
What's that?

96
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,640
What is that?

97
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,240
Is that an iceberg?

98
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,280
Is he a caveman?

99
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:23,960
Kankichi!

100
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:34,020
It really does shine differently.

101
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:37,100
Hey, Ryo-chan. Can I have a little too?

102
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,000
No way.

103
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,400
Why not? Just a little.

104
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,900
This precious ice was bought and cut overnight.
I'm not giving it away for free.

105
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:45,160
Stingy!

106
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:49,510
No matter what you say,
I've already paid Nakagawa ten thousand yen.

107
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,040
All the ice is mine.

108
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:57,660
You two deserve the refrigerator ice,
like Tenkichi-kun.

109
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:03,240
What a vulgar sound.

110
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:07,860
Compared to that what a wonderful sound!

111
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,260
It's like the chirping of a bell cricket.

112
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:13,380
This is authentic,
traditional Japanese shaved ice!

113
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,600
Now just pour on the syrup,

114
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:16,720
and it's done.

115
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:16,920
Done!

116
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:22,220
The ice itself is delicate and beautiful,
like light snow.

117
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:24,100
First, one bite.

118
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,920
Delicious!

119
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,120
Real ice really is different!

120
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,780
Compared to that,

121
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:37,720
this smell,
a mix of tap water chlorine and fridge odor,

122
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,340
is truly unpleasant.

123
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,150
Mm,

124
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,800
this deliciousness!

125
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:50,920
It can only come from ice that's beautiful,
secret, and bold, full of ancient romance.

126
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,320
The finest shaved ice in the world,
the shaved ice of shaved ice!

127
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:57,940
No, in fact,
only this should be called shaved ice.

128
00:07:59,020 --> 00:07:59,380
Yeah.

129
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:05,280
Shaved fridge ice made for
free is no longer shaved ice.

130
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:10,160
Yesterday you were eating what Pen-kichi made and calling it the best,
you know.

131
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:14,500
That's it, next time let's
make it luxuriously with milk.

132
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:21,880
Don't go stealing ice without permission,
or I'll arrest you!

133
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:23,980
Just a little wouldn't hurt!

134
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:27,940
I'm directing traffic in this heat,
so this iceberg is my reward.

135
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:30,860
Look, the cars are honking!
Hurry up and get to work.

136
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,760
Stingy!

137
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,000
Beautiful.

138
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,560
Delicious.

139
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,120
Truly delicious.

140
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,000
This is truly gourmet shaved ice.

141
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:56,940
I wish I could let you two have a taste.

142
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,680
To be satisfied with
that kind of shaved ice...

143
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,000
How truly pitiful.

144
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:05,200
The sparkle of the ice
and its silky smoothness.

145
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,260
That crisp,
popping sound of the ice shattering...

146
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:11,100
Awakened from a slumber
of millions of years.

147
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:14,320
It has the elegance of Venus's whisper.

148
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,120
Fantastic!

149
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,260
This picture is rose-colored,
kakezōri-colored.

150
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:24,360
I'm gonna eat it all up!

151
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,420
Ahhhhhh.

152
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,640
My head's gone numb from the cold!

153
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:36,000
But by the seventieth bowl,

154
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,800
you're getting tired of it, aren't you?
Isn't it about time

155
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:40,280
As if that could happen!

156
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,680
So this is what they call iceberg ice

157
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,320
It's really cold, isn't it?

158
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,720
Hey!

159
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,660
It's dangerous, so get out of the way!

160
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,040
Feels so good, doesn't it?

161
00:09:56,020 --> 00:10:01,900
Hey! This is my ice! Don't you dare
go sticking to it without permission!

162
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:05,600
I paid a fortune for this!
It's a whole week's worth of food for me!

163
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:14,440
A big serving of Delicious!

164
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,800
Strawberry with milk topping, how dashing!

165
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,520
I ate it all at once and
now my head's gone numb!

166
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,760
Are you all right, senpai?

167
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:34,580
Don't push yourself. Why don't
you hand some out to the neighbors?

168
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:37,200
P-pfft, this is nothing...

169
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:40,060
If I think of this stuff as just water,
I can fit in as much as I want!

170
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:43,560
Two-thirds of the human body is water,
after all.

171
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:47,880
There's still this much left,
from just one little chunk...

172
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,400
Alright!
I'll give you two a special service too!

173
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,140
I'll give you some of this
authentic gourmet shaved ice.

174
00:10:54,140 --> 00:10:56,200
No, that's okay, we already ate.

175
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,700
Right, we don't want any.

176
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,620
Ryo-chan, you'd better take responsibility.

177
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:02,000
Fine, I'll just eat it all, okay?

178
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,840
I'll eat it all out of sheer spite!

179
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,720
What do you think you're doing?

180
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:17,400
Isn't it obvious?

181
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:18,660
I'm going to eat it.

182
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:21,420
Strawberry and milk flavors are all there is,
so I get bored of them.

183
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:25,400
For this part, I'll pour on some cola
and add a twist with ketchup sauce.

184
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,900
Over here,
I'll drop a raw egg and natto on top.

185
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,540
And to top it off,
I'll add some nutrition with vitamin drink.

186
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,340
How about that? Looks delicious, right?

187
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,660
You're really going to eat that?

188
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:35,780
Of course.

189
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,260
Just watching makes me want to throw up.

190
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:51,600
It's getting cold.

191
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:54,520
Let's drink some tea to warm our bodies up.

192
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,400
Alright, I'm nice and warm now.

193
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,880
I can't do it, I can't eat any more.

194
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,420
So what are you going to do with the rest?

195
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:17,020
I'll make it into rice
balls and eat them later.

196
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:19,540
What is this?!

197
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:23,460
Ryotsu! Is this your doing again?!

198
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:26,040
W-what? I didn't do anything...

199
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,960
You idiot! Get over here!

200
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,180
Ow ow!

201
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:31,280
Wait, my ear is stretching!

202
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:36,560
What is this ice?! That phone has
been ringing nonstop with complaints!

203
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,820
No, th-this is

204
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:42,340
It's a stage set I prepared for you, Chief!

205
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,920
For me?

206
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,978
That's right.
With this iceberg as the backdrop,

207
00:12:47,028 --> 00:12:51,840
I thought you could sing your favorite
"Drifting Ice Floe Journey" at karaoke.

208
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,060
Don't try to change the subject!

209
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:58,060
This Arctic ice was imported
directly from Greenland.

210
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:01,000
Ryo-chan bought it from
Kei-chan for ten thousand yen.

211
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:02,800
Ryotsu!

212
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,900
Would you like a cup too, Chief?

213
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,200
I don't want any!

214
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:12,480
Get rid of this ice! Understand? Today!

215
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,200
Today, you say...

216
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,500
Shut up!

217
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,800
If this ice isn't
completely gone by tomorrow,

218
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:22,360
you're being transferred
to the Arctic Police Box!

219
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:26,120
Wh-what?
Does an Arctic Police Box even exist?

220
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,700
I'll set one up especially for you.

221
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,000
Got it, Ryotsu?

222
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,340
Still, there's quite a lot of it left

223
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:50,380
There's no way we can eat all of this today.

224
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,200
So this is it?

225
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,720
The iceberg Ryo-san bought

226
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,600
is a genuine Arctic iceberg.

227
00:13:57,600 --> 00:14:01,040
Standing out like this, word spreads fast.

228
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,540
What were you thinking,
buying something like this?

229
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:07,060
I was going to turn it all
into shaved ice and eat it.

230
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,300
Shaved ice?

231
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:13,700
If you shave this much ice,
you could even go skiing on it.

232
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,700
That's it, that's it!

233
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:21,120
Skiing in this damn hot midsummer,
how sweet!

234
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:23,020
This is going to be a hit.

235
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,340
Rental skis and rental snowboards.

236
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,300
Rubber sledding could work, too.

237
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:36,280
We'll make money and get rid of the ice.

238
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:37,820
Two birds with one stone.

239
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:40,200
Right, let's get started right away.

240
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:48,140
Here we go.

241
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,480
What's this?

242
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,080
Even if my hands get dirty,

243
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:10,500
I wonder what Senpai is
planning to start this time.

244
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,900
One thing's for sure, money's involved.

245
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:16,560
Ryo-chan's energy comes from
nothing but making money.

246
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:34,580
Good work.

247
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,240
Keep bringing the rest over quickly.

248
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:37,780
Coming, Ryo-san!

249
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:38,800
Leave it to me.

250
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,540
Once the scaffolding's up,
next comes the sheet!

251
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:42,220
OK.

252
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:44,500
This is a piece of cake.

253
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:55,560
With this, the road's open now, right?

254
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:58,260
What is Kankichi doing with that ice?

255
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,320
It's coming along nicely.

256
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,260
Aaaaah!

257
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:16,080
I brought the skis and snowboards.

258
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:19,320
Aaaah, just put them over there, OK?

259
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,040
Okay, that's the setup done.
Not bad, if I do say so myself.

260
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:34,300
Step right up, step right up!

261
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,700
Ryotsu Snowland!

262
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:37,560
We're now open for business!

263
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,640
What's this
"Ryotsu Snowland" supposed to be?

264
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:42,020
Come on over, come on over and see!

265
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:44,340
Snow is falling in Katsushika
in the middle of summer!

266
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:46,540
In the great city, a desert-like metropolis,

267
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:48,040
the Karuizawa of the old downtown!

268
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:52,200
In the height of this midsummer heat,
skiing and snowboarding,

269
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:54,940
and even bobsledding,
you can enjoy it all here and nowhere else!

270
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,000
Step right up, step right up!

271
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,020
Let's go in and check it out!

272
00:16:58,020 --> 00:16:59,800
Yeah, sounds like fun.

273
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,780
Me too.

274
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:04,704
The traffic jam has cleared up, but

275
00:17:04,754 --> 00:17:07,200
there's still quite a lot left

276
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:12,200
Alright, alright, rentals this way! Bring-your-own
gear is spill-over-the-edge, no charge!

277
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:15,045
Yes, group discount is 10% off! Young man,

278
00:17:15,095 --> 00:17:18,080
young lady, grandpa and grandma get 30% off!

279
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:19,000
Come on, how about it?

280
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:20,280
That snowboard there!

281
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,110
Alright, alright, welcome, welcome!

282
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,600
Welcome!

283
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:26,360
Go on, go on!

284
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,060
Thanks a lot!

285
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,180
This must be worth a few million, I'd say.

286
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,880
Right, let's set up some food stalls too!

287
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,980
Come on, come on, stop by!

288
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:41,260
If you're hungry,
try Snowland's famous ice sushi!

289
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,980
Fatty tuna and squid that'll
make Mom and Dad weep with joy!

290
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:46,080
Sweet rolled omelet, the kids' favorite!

291
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,740
If you don't eat these,
you've wasted your trip here!

292
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:51,040
Then make me one, fatty tuna!

293
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,340
I'll have the egg!

294
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,080
Seriously nutritious!

295
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,900
The rice part is made of shaved ice.

296
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,400
And the topping stays cold,
so it lasts longer.

297
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,080
How do you eat it?

298
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,900
Like this, you dip it in jam and eat it.

299
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:15,400
It goes down light and easy.

300
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:17,040
Jam sushi, come on!

301
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:19,120
For those who can't stand raw stuff,

302
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:22,000
How about ice curry?
Even Indians would be amazed!

303
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,240
Come on, step right up!

304
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,040
Even the curry is ice!

305
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,840
I want that one!

306
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,280
Curry-itcha!

307
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,900
I could keep going forever!

308
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,880
Come on, come on, the things you dropped,
I'll give them away for free!

309
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,460
Sorry for bumping you,
the cars and balls too!

310
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,160
Throw and be happy,
it's Smoke Pitcher Tokura!

311
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:48,780
Mister, give me one!

312
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:49,180
Me too!

313
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:50,240
Me too!

314
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:51,680
Alright, alright, no pushing!

315
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,600
Balls are 200 yen here!

316
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:56,660
Whoa! They sold out fast!

317
00:18:57,580 --> 00:19:01,100
Already sold out You
can't beat this business.

318
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:09,260
What? What's that? Ryotsu's doing what?

319
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,544
Making a Snowland in the
park without permission,

320
00:19:12,594 --> 00:19:14,200
and gathering customers.

321
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,020
Apparently he's renting skis
and snowboards to make money.

322
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:21,020
What a guy, honestly!

323
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,260
Yeah, yeah.

324
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:27,300
If it's this profitable,
should I buy another iceberg's worth of ice?

325
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:28,880
Alright!

326
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,760
Y-yes, Chief? What is it?

327
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:41,000
I hear you've been secretly setting up this kind
of thing in the park and making money off it.

328
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,440
Absolutely not!

329
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:45,400
I wasn't just getting rid of the ice,

330
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:48,420
I wanted to create a place for
interaction with the local residents,

331
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:52,180
I just wanted the people of Kameari to be happy.
That's all.

332
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:54,740
Then what's this?

333
00:19:56,640 --> 00:20:00,720
Ryotsu! I know you've got
the money hidden behind you!

334
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,520
Give it back to everyone right now!

335
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:04,700
No way, I'm not doing that!

336
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,200
Wait!

337
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,860
Time-out, time-out!

338
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,100
Timeout!

339
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:12,820
Wait!

340
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,260
That went well.

341
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,600
It won't come off.

342
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,740
There's egg too!

343
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:33,880
Wasabi.

344
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,600
Hey, get back here!

345
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:44,260
Wait!

346
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,060
Damn it!

347
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:58,740
Whoa, no way!

348
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:02,820
Bishi-tah!

349
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,260
Hold it!

350
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:15,100
Watch out!

351
00:21:16,140 --> 00:21:21,880
Damn it!

352
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:26,420
This is mine. I'm not giving it to anyone!

353
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:29,220
Swing, swing, swing, swing!

354
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,540
You little...!

355
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,660
Prepare yourself, Ryotsu!

356
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,240
No way!

357
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:41,640
Not so fast!

358
00:21:57,540 --> 00:22:00,540
It's collapsing!

359
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:28,160


360
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,880
Where did everyone go?

361
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:33,340
It's handover time, though.

362
00:22:33,340 --> 00:22:38,680
Whoa, the two of you!

363
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:45,540
That's strange, no one's here at all.

364
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:49,240
Chief!

365
00:22:58,660 --> 00:22:59,760
Help!

366
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,740
Help!

367
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,840
I held on to it!

368
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:26,100
This money has to be returned to everyone.

369
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:28,620
No way! It's mine!

370
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,355
Wh

371
00:23:31,405 --> 00:23:34,240
Ha-ki ha

372
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:43,120
Well, that's good.
You got to use up all the ice.

373
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:47,680
He's a stingy guy who squeezes every last bit out of anything he paid for himself,
after all.

374
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:50,160
I suppose it's instinct driving him.

375
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,680
Shut up!

376
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,360
Whew, I'm beat, I'm beat.

377
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:08,960
Make Reikon angry and
you'll get a horrible fate.

378
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:11,880
He throws expressways and
sucks away mini-putters.

379
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,760
He drives the expressway the wrong way.

380
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:16,100
With that, no one would want to marry him.

381
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:20,500
Next time: Reikon's Furious Great Chase,
see you then!

382
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:36,760
Let's always smile, okay?

383
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:40,960
Even if something outrageous happens,

384
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:45,460
keep smiling cutely, okay?

385
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:50,700
just head out with a carefree face.

386
00:24:50,700 --> 00:24:54,200
Hey, smile for me.

387
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,500
It's not your fault.

388
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:06,600
Hey, smile for me,
like you were a moment ago, yeah!

389
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:16,640
Keep smiling all the time, because a
woman who acts serious isn't beautiful.

390
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:25,900
You should smile right away,
unless you're a child.

391
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:40,900
Thank you for watching.

